.TH COF-SETUP 1 "2026-11-13" "cof 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cof-setup \- Interactive setup wizard
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
cof setup [OPTIONS]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Interactive setup wizard: detects reachable backends (Ollama, ComfyUI), picks
a default adapter and model, and writes ~/.config/circuitry/config.json (and,
for a detected API key, ~/.config/circuitry/.env).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --json
Output detection results as JSON (non-interactive).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B cof setup
Runs the interactive setup wizard.
.TP
.B cof setup --json
Detects backends and prints the result as JSON, non-interactively.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_CONFIG
Not consulted by setup itself; setup always writes the global config.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/circuitry/config.json
Written with the detected/chosen adapter and model.
.TP
.I ~/.config/circuitry/.env
Written with a detected API key, when setup finds one.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The command failed, or the input was invalid.
.TP
.B 2
A usage error -- an unrecognized option or missing argument.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBcof(1)\fR, \fBcof-doctor(1)\fR, \fBcof-init(1)\fR
